'One static photographic enlargement and empty-print drying preparation workcorner, using three complete existing qualified models and zero new independent models. A whole raised crank desk is rigidly turned ninety degrees as one unchanged instance. The complete downward-bellows enlarger rests with its entire finite lower base face on the real desk top. Beside it, the whole six-tray cantilever open-mesh rack stands separately on the scene-only floor, with its empty front access facing the work area. No tray, column, camera part or table component is extracted, rescaled, recoloured or counted as a new prop. All original local GLB coordinates, normals, hierarchy and full PBR are preserved; only one unit-scale rigid parent rotation and translations place the complete originals. This is a dry equipment-preparation layout, not the existing camera shooting studio or film-rewind inspection bench. No chemical baths, liquids, paper, image, red safelight or working darkroom process is supplied. Static composition only: no optical exposure, photographic development, drying effectiveness, equipment fit, ergonomic access, actual lifting, load, stability, chemical or electrical safety claim. No rigging, animation or interaction.'
